{
 "note": "Captured once from the published effect-dynamodb@1.40.0 and @effect-dynamodb/schema@1.40.0, installed outside the repo and run by a scratch script against DynamoDB Local. Two aggregates on one table, each listed by tournament on gsi1: Matches, whose root holds structs that rename their keys on encode (Schema.encodeKeys): meta { amount -> am, tags -> tg, note }, swap { a -> b, b -> a }, outer { inner -> in: { deep -> dp }, list: [{ deep -> dp }] }, recs (a record of { deep -> dp }), either (meta or a struct holding amount as amount), maybe (optional, nullable meta), and plain { x, ys } that renames nothing; and Games, whose root renames nothing. Two of each are created (m1 / m2, g1 / g2). For each list filter, spelled by stored names and by domain names: its outcome and every request the list sent, whole, in order; the table's name is <table>, UUIDs <token> and timestamps <time>. Never regenerate it: it is the record of what 1.40.0 did.",
